1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,667
One of the things that —

2
00:00:03,367 --> 00:00:08,700
let's say — makes you unaware of what is expected of you. You mentioned,

3
00:00:08,733 --> 00:00:12,600
Abu Badr, “success” more than once. But when I

4
00:00:12,633 --> 00:00:15,800
spoke to you once on the phone, you told me: “al-falāḥ.”

5
00:00:17,833 --> 00:00:21,833
You didn't use it [since] — you used it once in conversation. Could we bring it back here,

6
00:00:21,867 --> 00:00:26,400
on this very network — I mean defining it as a concept? I expected you today

7
00:00:26,433 --> 00:00:29,067
to bring up al-falāḥ, but I decided to remind you of

8
00:00:29,100 --> 00:00:32,567
the topic. You spoke about it on the phone quickly

9
00:00:32,600 --> 00:00:36,167
and in passing, but it captivated me — when you said “the concept of al-falāḥ”

10
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:41,600
and so on. I want to understand what's meant by it. In our own framework —

11
00:00:41,633 --> 00:00:46,133
we refer back to our lexicon, to our frame of reference — what is

12
00:00:46,167 --> 00:00:49,267
the concept of al-falāḥ? And how… because today there is this standard of “success” (najjāḥ) —

13
00:00:49,300 --> 00:00:51,300
even that standard is unclear: what is success? I,

14
00:00:51,333 --> 00:00:53,300
to this day, don't know exactly what success is. When you set out to define it —

15
00:00:53,333 --> 00:00:55,867
your success may be different from mine. But I expect that

16
00:00:55,900 --> 00:00:59,767
al-falāḥ, according to our frame of reference, should be the [true] concept.

17
00:00:59,800 --> 00:01:03,633
— Beautiful! What do you think? Beautiful, excellent. Now, “success” (najjāḥ)

18
00:01:03,667 --> 00:01:08,767
in the language — any concept, of course… how do concepts come to be?

19
00:01:08,800 --> 00:01:14,033
Concepts are meanings that people express, then settle upon by convention,

20
00:01:14,067 --> 00:01:19,067
so a meaning becomes a term; then they assign it a definition — called

21
00:01:19,100 --> 00:01:23,600
a definition or a “ḥadd” (precise delimiting definition). So these definitions

22
00:01:23,633 --> 00:01:26,367
must be taken from the language at the outset. What does the language say?

23
00:01:26,400 --> 00:01:31,300
What is the definition of success? “Najaḥa” means: he attained his goal.

24
00:01:31,333 --> 00:01:35,800
That is, it has two parts: a goal, and an act.

25
00:01:35,833 --> 00:01:40,467
“He attained his goal” — so it is a conception (taṣawwur)

26
00:01:40,500 --> 00:01:41,633
and a conduct (taṣarruf).

27
00:01:43,533 --> 00:01:45,833
In our framework, for there to be success and falāḥ,

28
00:01:47,067 --> 00:01:51,500
we have not two things but three: that you have

29
00:01:51,533 --> 00:01:56,067
striving (saʿy), awareness (waʿy) and revelation (wahy) — yes!

30
00:01:56,100 --> 00:01:59,067
Our triad: striving, revelation

31
00:01:59,100 --> 00:02:03,733
and awareness. Success is

32
00:02:03,767 --> 00:02:08,633
attaining what is sought — attaining one's goal; that is success. Therefore, the definition of

33
00:02:08,667 --> 00:02:14,033
success is: achieving what YOU want. And the definition of

34
00:02:14,067 --> 00:02:18,567
al-falāḥ is: achieving what Allah wants FROM you. That is al-falāḥ.

35
00:02:18,600 --> 00:02:23,900
So if you achieve the first at the expense of the second, then that is

36
00:02:23,933 --> 00:02:28,533
failure. And if you achieve the second, even if the first is absent, that is

37
00:02:28,567 --> 00:02:34,033
the pinnacle of success — al-falāḥ. And if there come together for you

38
00:02:34,067 --> 00:02:38,733
success along with falāḥ, then you are in an earthly

39
00:02:38,767 --> 00:02:43,033
paradise. ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz says in a wondrous saying:

40
00:02:43,067 --> 00:02:48,467
“The sweetest life is one in harmony with obedience.” Amazing — you love

41
00:02:48,500 --> 00:02:52,833
something, and it is obedience, and Allah loves it: that is the most beloved thing — the most beautiful

42
00:02:52,867 --> 00:02:56,667
thing you could do. Here, success and al-falāḥ are united.
